UPDATE product SET description = 'A librarian named Nora finds herself in a vast library between life and death, where each book lets her live out a different version of her life. Matt Haig''s novel is about regret and the countless paths not taken, and what it actually takes to feel at home in the one you''re living.' WHERE id = 172;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Tara Westover''s memoir traces her childhood in a survivalist Mormon family in rural Idaho, with no birth certificate and no classroom until she was seventeen. It follows her unlikely path from that isolation to a PhD from Cambridge, and the cost of leaving a family behind to get there.' WHERE id = 173;
UPDATE product SET description = 'A psychological thriller about Alicia Berenson, a painter who shoots her husband and then never speaks another word. Her therapist becomes obsessed with uncovering the truth behind her silence, in a story that keeps its central twist hidden until the final pages.' WHERE id = 174;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Nobel laureate Daniel Kahneman lays out the two systems that drive how we think: one fast and intuitive, the other slow and deliberate. Drawing on decades of behavioral research, it explains the predictable ways both systems lead us into biased, sometimes costly judgments.' WHERE id = 175;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Andy Weir''s sci-fi novel follows Ryland Grace, who wakes up alone on a spacecraft with no memory of how he got there or why he''s the last hope for saving Earth. It''s a story about problem-solving under pressure, told with the same hard-science detail as Weir''s The Martian.' WHERE id = 176;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Paulo Coelho''s allegorical novel follows Santiago, an Andalusian shepherd boy, on a journey across the desert to the Egyptian pyramids in search of a treasure he saw in a recurring dream. Along the way it becomes less about the treasure and more about listening to what the book calls your Personal Legend.' WHERE id = 177;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Delia Owens'' novel follows Kya Clark, abandoned as a child to raise herself alone in the marshes of the North Carolina coast. When a local man is found dead, the story of her isolated life becomes tangled up with a murder investigation.' WHERE id = 178;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Don Norman''s classic on design explains why some everyday objects are intuitive to use and others leave you baffled by a door or a light switch. It''s a foundational read on usability and human-centered design, still assigned in design courses decades after it was first published.' WHERE id = 179;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Robert C. Martin lays out the principles behind software that stays maintainable as it grows -- separating business rules from frameworks, databases, and UI so that none of those details can lock a system in. It''s a widely referenced guide to structuring codebases for long-term change.' WHERE id = 180;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Frank Herbert''s science fiction epic follows Paul Atreides on the desert planet Arrakis, the only source of the universe''s most valuable resource, spice. It''s a story of political betrayal, ecology, and prophecy that''s shaped nearly every major sci-fi epic that followed it.' WHERE id = 181;
UPDATE product SET description = 'George Orwell''s dystopian novel imagines a totalitarian future under constant surveillance by the Party and Big Brother, where even private thought is a crime. Winston Smith''s quiet rebellion against that control has made the book''s language -- doublethink, thoughtcrime, Big Brother -- part of everyday vocabulary.' WHERE id = 182;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Harper Lee''s novel is narrated by Scout Finch, a young girl in Depression-era Alabama, as her father Atticus defends a Black man falsely accused of a crime. It''s a story about prejudice and moral courage seen through a child''s eyes.' WHERE id = 183;
UPDATE product SET description = 'J.R.R. Tolkien''s fantasy novel follows Bilbo Baggins, a hobbit pulled out of his comfortable life on a quest with a company of dwarves to reclaim their homeland from the dragon Smaug. It''s the standalone adventure that set up everything that followed in The Lord of the Rings.' WHERE id = 184;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Charles Duhigg breaks down the science of how habits form -- the cue, routine, and reward loop -- and how that loop can be deliberately changed. It draws on real cases from individuals, companies, and organizations to show habits being rebuilt in practice, not just theory.' WHERE id = 185;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Peter Thiel''s book on startups argues that real progress comes from doing something genuinely new (going from zero to one) rather than copying what already works (going from one to n). It''s part startup playbook, part argument for contrarian thinking.' WHERE id = 186;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Eric Ries lays out the build-measure-learn loop for startups: ship a minimum viable product, learn from real customers fast, and adjust course before running out of resources. It became one of the defining playbooks for startup methodology in the years after its release.' WHERE id = 187;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Viktor Frankl, a psychiatrist and Holocaust survivor, draws on his time in Nazi concentration camps to argue that meaning -- not pleasure or power -- is what allows people to endure even the worst suffering. Part memoir and part introduction to his logotherapy approach to psychology.' WHERE id = 188;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Mark Manson''s self-help book pushes back on relentless positivity, arguing that a good life comes from choosing carefully what to care about rather than trying to care about everything. It''s blunt and profanity-laced by design, a deliberate contrast to more conventional self-help.' WHERE id = 189;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Robert Kiyosaki contrasts the financial lessons from his own father with those of his best friend''s father, using the two to argue for building assets and financial literacy over simply working for a paycheck. It''s one of the best-selling personal finance books ever published, still recommended and debated today.' WHERE id = 190;
UPDATE product SET description = 'J.D. Salinger''s novel follows Holden Caulfield over a few days in New York after he''s expelled from prep school, drifting through the city while railing against what he sees as the phoniness of the adult world. Its voice -- restless, cynical, achingly sincere -- made it a defining portrait of teenage alienation.' WHERE id = 191;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Aldous Huxley''s dystopian novel imagines a future society engineered for stability through genetic conditioning, a caste system decided before birth, and a drug called soma that keeps everyone content. It''s less about overt oppression than about a population that''s been conditioned not to want anything different.' WHERE id = 192;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Cormac McCarthy''s novel follows a father and son walking south through a burned, post-apocalyptic America, carrying nothing but each other and what little they can scavenge. Sparse and bleak, it''s ultimately a story about protecting a child in a world that''s given up nearly every reason to.' WHERE id = 193;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Haruki Murakami''s novel follows Toru Watanabe as he looks back on his student years in 1960s Tokyo, caught between two very different women while grieving the death of a close friend. It''s a quieter, more grounded story than much of Murakami''s other work, focused on memory, loss, and first love.' WHERE id = 194;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Andy Weir''s debut novel follows astronaut Mark Watney, stranded alone on Mars after his crew assumes he''s dead, as he uses botany, chemistry, and sheer stubbornness to survive until a rescue might be possible. It balances real scientific problem-solving with a persistently dark sense of humor.' WHERE id = 195;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Madeline Miller retells the Greek myth of Circe, the witch banished to a solitary island by the gods, giving her a voice and interior life the original myths never bothered with. It follows her across centuries of Greek mythology, from Prometheus to the Odyssey and beyond.' WHERE id = 196;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Erin Morgenstern''s fantasy novel centers on Le Cirque des Rêves, a circus that only opens at night, and the two young magicians bound in a competition neither of them fully understands the rules of. It''s built more around atmosphere and imagery than plot momentum, a slow immersive read.' WHERE id = 197;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Amor Towles'' novel follows Count Alexander Rostov, sentenced by a Bolshevik tribunal to house arrest for life inside Moscow''s Metropol Hotel. Confined to one building for decades, he builds a full life within it, and the novel becomes a meditation on dignity and purpose under confinement.' WHERE id = 198;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Khaled Hosseini''s novel follows Amir, a boy in Kabul, and his friendship with Hassan, the son of his father''s servant, and the betrayal that haunts Amir into adulthood. Set against decades of Afghanistan''s history, it''s a story about guilt and the possibility of redemption.' WHERE id = 199;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Yann Martel''s novel follows Pisc­ine "Pi" Patel, a shipwreck survivor stranded on a lifeboat in the Pacific with an unlikely companion: a Bengal tiger named Richard Parker. Part survival story, part meditation on faith and storytelling, it asks which version of events you''d rather believe.' WHERE id = 200;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Paula Hawkins'' psychological thriller follows Rachel, who watches a seemingly perfect couple from the train each day, until one of them goes missing and Rachel realizes she may have seen something important. Told through unreliable narrators, it keeps the reader guessing along with them.' WHERE id = 201;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Gillian Flynn''s thriller opens with Amy Dunne''s disappearance on her fifth wedding anniversary, with all evidence pointing to her husband Nick. Told from both their perspectives, it''s less a whodunit than a slow unraveling of a marriage built on lies.' WHERE id = 202;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Set in Nazi Germany and narrated by Death itself, Markus Zusak''s novel follows Liesel Meminger, a foster girl who steals books and shares them with her neighbors during air raids. It''s a story about the power of words in a time when they were being burned and banned.' WHERE id = 203;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Ray Bradbury''s dystopian novel imagines a future where books are outlawed and "firemen" burn any that are found, following one fireman, Guy Montag, who starts questioning why. It remains one of the most widely read warnings about censorship and a society that''s stopped reading.' WHERE id = 204;
UPDATE product SET description = 'John Green''s YA novel follows Hazel and Augustus, two teenagers who meet in a cancer support group and fall in love despite -- and because of -- knowing how little time they may have. It''s sharply funny as often as it''s devastating, refusing to soften either side.' WHERE id = 205;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Michelle Obama''s memoir traces her path from the South Side of Chicago to Princeton, Harvard Law, and eventually the White House as First Lady. It''s a personal account of identity and public life, and of building a career and a family under constant public scrutiny.' WHERE id = 206;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Malcolm Gladwell argues that success has less to do with individual talent than with timing, culture, and the thousands of hours of practice behind it -- the book''s "10,000-hour rule" became a cultural shorthand for mastery. It draws on examples from hockey players to Bill Gates to make its case.' WHERE id = 207;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Clayton Christensen''s business classic explains why successful, well-run companies keep losing to smaller competitors with cheaper, simpler technology, coining the term "disruptive innovation" in the process. It''s one of the most influential business books of the last thirty years, still cited constantly in tech and strategy circles.' WHERE id = 208;
UPDATE product SET description = 'Aditya Bhargava''s illustrated guide walks through core algorithms -- binary search, sorting, graph algorithms, dynamic programming -- using hand-drawn diagrams and plain language instead of dense pseudocode. It''s aimed at programmers who want the intuition behind an algorithm, not just the implementation.' WHERE id = 209;
